Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Forward Deployed Engineer* role at *Assort Health*. At Sperse, I built a production Python, FastAPI, and LangGraph platform that routes work across 40+ specialized AI agents with secure access controls for 10,000+ users. I also delivered a monitored FastMCP integration layer exposing 160+ backend actions, enabling AI agents to automate customer CRM workflows securely across multiple tenants. To give users control over those systems, I built a React, TypeScript, and Temporal interface for configuring, launching, monitoring, and resuming long-running agent workflows. That combination of production AI-agent engineering, backend APIs and integrations, and customer workflow ownership aligns directly with Assort's need for an engineer who can carry complex implementations from technical scoping through go-live and optimization.

My work has required the same operational discipline that successful healthcare deployments demand. I used Claude Code and Codex CLI to automate deployment pipelines, error monitoring, and automated testing, then added OpenTelemetry trace-based evaluations to GitHub Actions CI/CD so latency, accuracy, and safety issues could be caught before releases reached users. I also integrated OpenAI Codex with Bitbucket to automate triage across 25–30 pull requests each week, saving reviewers several hours of manual effort. Earlier at Qualitest, I built a cloud-agnostic Java and Spring Boot API across S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO, and improved timeout recovery across 100K+ weekly executions with AWS Step Functions. These systems taught me to make failure visible, preserve recovery paths, and build interfaces that technical and business stakeholders can understand. To demonstrate how I approach an ambiguous implementation gap, I published Care Deploy Evidence, an offline-first five-stage LangGraph and FastAPI workflow that analyzes requirements, maps supplied evidence, exposes gaps, generates grounded bullets, and validates each claim. The project provides both a CLI and FastAPI interface, structured stage logs, sensitive-claim safeguards, and GitHub Actions CI. Its 18-test suite passes at 97.98% coverage, and its sample report truthfully supports 9 of 10 requirement categories rather than hiding the unsupported healthcare-systems gap. That evidence-first design reflects how I would approach customer discovery and production deployment: make assumptions explicit, connect requirements to implementation facts, and surface risk early.

Assort's goal of *Building Healthcare That Remembers*—creating one continuous conversation across the patient journey—is a compelling use of production AI. I would bring an ownership mindset consistent with *Answer the Call* and a customer-centered *5-Star Focus*: listening closely to technical and nontechnical stakeholders, translating workflow constraints into reliable systems, debugging issues through production launch, and turning patterns from individual deployments into reusable tooling. I would welcome the opportunity to work alongside customers, Product, and Engineering to help Assort launch AI agents that make patient access more continuous and dependable. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration; I look forward to connecting.

